NOTABLE_GAPS:
Empty or thin cells: religion in 2017 (Pasternack, 'Restoring Kant's Conception of the Highest Good', JHP 2017, was screened out on per-year cap; Kanterian's Kant, God and Metaphysics is dated 2017 by CrossRef online and 2018 by the SEP bibliography and was not included); the Opus postumum in 2018 (Huseyinzadegan in Rethinking Kant 5 was seen but carries few indicators); animals in 2016 and 2017 (Fisher, 'Kant on Animal Minds', Ergo 2017, screened out); gender in 2016 and 2018 (Huseyinzadegan on the Kantian feminist, Feminist Philosophy Quarterly 2018, screened out); education and pedagogy in all three years (Louden, 'Total Transformation: Why Kant Did Not Give up on Education', Kantian Review 2016, screened out); neo-Kantian reception (Beiser's Hermann Cohen, 2018, is a biography of Cohen rather than a Kant study; Gironi's Sellars and Meillassoux volume, 2017, reviewed in NDPR, was screened out); aesthetics proper in 2016; science and mathematics in 2016 beyond McNulty (Carson and Shabel (eds.), Kant: Studies on Mathematics in the Critical Philosophy, 2016, appears in the SEP kant-mathematics bibliography but could not be verified with CrossRef or S2 in this session and is therefore excluded); Metaphysics of Morals and virtue as a monograph topic in 2016 and 2018 beyond the edition and Merritt. No NDPR review was found for Rauscher, Hoewing, Gomes and Stephenson, Flikschuh, Papish, Holtman, Horstmann, Denis or the Religion edition, so those rest on citations, SEP listings and publisher or series status.
CONSIDERED_NOT_INCLUDED (with reasons): Wilson, Kantian Review 2016 (inclination), Mudd, EJP 2016, Golob, Kantian Review 2016, Gomes, Mind 2016, O'Neill, Kant-Studien 2016, Gava, Pragmatism Kant and Transcendental Philosophy (online 2015), Eldridge, Images of History (2016; Kant and Benjamin, reviewed in NDPR by Velkley), Faggion et al., Kant and Social Policies (2016), Kisilevsky and Stone, Freedom and Force (2017; NDPR review by Ripstein), Timmons, Significance and System (2017; NDPR review by Bader; a collection of reprinted essays), Formosa, Kantian Ethics Dignity and Perfection (2017), Wood, Formulas of the Moral Law (2017, Cambridge Element), Kazim, Kant on Conscience (2017), Altman (ed.), The Palgrave Kant Handbook (2017), Watkins (ed.), Kant on Persons and Agency (2017-12), Schulting, Kant's Radical Subjectivism (2017), Tinguely (2017), Zammito, The Gestation of German Biology (CrossRef print 2017; Kant is one of several principal figures), Gironi (ed.), The Legacy of Kant in Sellars and Meillassoux (2017), Krasnoff et al., Kant's Doctrine of Right in the 21st Century (2018), Dyck and Wunderlich (eds.), Kant and his German Contemporaries (2 volumes, 2018; reviewed in NDPR), Rinne et al., Kant on Love (2018), Moran, Kant on Freedom and Spontaneity (2018), Forgione, Kant and the Problem of Self-Knowledge (2018), Glezer, Kant on Reality Cause and Force (2018), Westphal, Grounds of Pragmatic Realism (2018; Hegel is the main interlocutor), Beiser, Hermann Cohen (2018), Nunez (Mind 2018), Massimi (Synthese 2018), Timmermann (Kantian Review 2018), Peters (JHP 2018), Hasan (EJP 2018), and the remaining Kant-Studien and Kantian Review articles of each year, all screened out on indicators or on the per-year cap.
INCOMPLETE ENTRIES: one article, mills2018radical (Black Radical Kantianism; S2, OpenAlex and CORE returned no abstract; the SUMMARY rests on the PhilPapers snippet, tagged summary-source-philpapers-snippet). No book is INCOMPLETE. Two books carry an NDPR review as their abstract source after the enrichment step (thorndike2017 and merritt2018; the S2 text for Merritt was the book's introduction and was replaced by the NDPR review, both checked against the book). The enrichment script's NDPR fuzzy match was run and attached only the correct review to thorndike2017. nassar2016analogical and varden2017women had no abstract through the DOI route; their abstracts were obtained by title search (CORE) and from the abstract resolver output saved earlier in the session. DOI handling: varden2017women carries the DOI in the url field rather than a doi field because CrossRef's first record year (2015, online-first) differs from the print year used here (2017, volume 98 issue 4); the metadata_cleaner simulation on a copy of the file reported 0 changes. Two raw JSON files from the earlier attempt (cr8_venue_kant_d3.json, ndpr_headers_d3.json) were moved out of intermediate_files/json to intermediate_files/d3/raw_json because their result structure crashes metadata_cleaner.py (results lists of strings).

SYNTHESIS_GUIDANCE:
Year sections can be organised by the subfield and debate tags; cross-reference Schulting, Conant, McLear (2016) and Watkins and Willaschek, O'Shea and Gomes and Stephenson (2017) for the conceptualism and perception line, Allais (2016), Valdez and Varden (2017) and Mills and Sandford (2018) for the race, colonialism and gender line, and Stang (2016) and Willaschek (2018) for the metaphysics line. Thorndike's CrossRef year (2017) differs from its publisher and NDPR year (2018); both fall in this block.

KEY_POSITIONS:
- Systematic reconstruction of Kant's metaphysics, modality and the Dialectic: Stang 2016, Willaschek 2018, Nisenbaum 2018.
- Cognition, perception and nonconceptualism: Schulting 2016, Conant 2016, McLear 2016, Watkins and Willaschek 2017, O'Shea 2017, Gomes and Stephenson 2017.
- Normativity, reflection and practical reason: Pollok 2017, Merritt 2018, Kleingeld 2017, Guyer 2016.
- Laws of nature, science and logic: Massimi and Breitenbach 2017, McNulty 2016, Lu-Adler 2018.
- Kant, race, colonialism, gender and animals: Allais 2016, Valdez 2017, Varden 2017, Korsgaard 2018, Mills 2018, Sandford 2018.
